    "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"h\",\n    \"v\",\n    \"e\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"der(h)\",\n    \"der(v)\",\n    \"v_new\",\n    \"e\",\n    \"_D_whenCondition1\"\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"In this scenario, the behavior of the FMU is probed by applying a combination of step, ramp, and sine excitations to the input variables. The input 'h' is subjected to a step function change at time 0.05s, representing a sudden change in height. The input 'v' is given a ramp function starting from 0 and increasing linearly up to 0.1 m/s by time 0.2s. Finally, a sine wave excitation is applied to the input 'e' with a frequency of 1Hz, simulating a periodic parameter input. Outputs like the derivatives of height and velocity ('der(h)' and 'der(v)') are tracked, along with the updated velocity state 'v_new' and the condition flag '_D_whenCondition1'. This setup provides insights into the dynamic response and state updates of the system under varying excitations.\"\n}\n```"
